// `_` is a legitimate value only of its own type (see unitResult.mln:
// `Result<_, E>` / `Ok(_)`), not a general-purpose placeholder: assigning it
// to an i32-declared variable is a type mismatch like any other, not the
// "undefined identifier" it would have been before `_` had a type of its
// own to infer.
i32 main() {
    i32 x = _;
    return x;
}
